meta {
  name: Subscribe Push
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/notifications/push/subscribe
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "endpoint": "https://fcm.googleapis.com/fcm/send/bruno-test-endpoint-001",
    "keys": {
      "p256dh": "BNcRdreALRFXTkOOUHK1EtK2wtaz5Ry4YfYCA_0QTpQtUbVlUls0VJXg7A8u-Ts1XbjhazAkj7I99e8QcYP7DkM",
      "auth": "tBHItJI5svbpez7KI4CCXg"
    },
    "user_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
  }
}

docs {
  The body carries ONLY the browser's PushSubscription. user/org/tenant come from
  the gateway-injected headers via parseAuthContext.

  `user_id` above is deliberately present and deliberately bogus: re-run this,
  then check that the stored row's user_id is the AUTHENTICATED user, not the
  forged one. Zod strips the unknown key before the handler ever sees it.

    SELECT user_id, org_id, endpoint FROM notify.push_subscriptions
    WHERE endpoint = 'https://fcm.googleapis.com/fcm/send/bruno-test-endpoint-001';

  Re-sending the same endpoint must UPDATE in place — one row, never two.
}
